/-!
# The compensated product of two mark profiles over a cell of a Lévy driver

For mark profiles `f, g : E → ℝ` and the representatives `J(h)`, for the joint filtration at `t`,
of the compensated integrals over the cell `(s, t]` that the cell increment
`levyCellProfileStep` uses as its jump coordinates, the compensated product over the cell is

  `Q(f, g) = J(f) J(g) − J(f g) − (t − s) ∫ f g dν`.

It agrees almost everywhere with `Poisson.compensatedProduct`, so at bounded square-integrable
profiles `f, g` it is square integrable and centred, its Gram is
`E[Q(f, g) Q(f', g')] = (t − s)² (⟨f, f'⟩ ⟨g, g'⟩ + ⟨f, g'⟩ ⟨g, f'⟩)` with `⟨u, v⟩ = ∫ u v dν`,
and it is orthogonal in `L²(P)` to every jump coordinate of the cell increment, whose profile need
only be square integrable. When `f`, `g` and `f g` are among the profiles of the cell increment,
the compensated product is measurable for the σ-algebra the cell increment generates.

The compensated integral of a square-integrable profile is an `L²(P)` limit of compensated step
integrals, each measurable for the counts of the Poisson random measure, so it is almost
everywhere equal to a function measurable for the σ-algebra of the Poisson random measure; so is
the compensated product of a square-integrable profile and a bounded square-integrable one, whose
product is square integrable. That σ-algebra is independent of the Brownian motion, so the
compensated product is independent of every Brownian increment of the cell, and a centred
Brownian increment is orthogonal to it.

## Main definitions

* `LevyStochCalc.Driver.levyCellProduct` — the compensated product of two mark profiles over a
  cell, built from the jump coordinates of the cell increment.

## Main statements

* `LevyStochCalc.Driver.levyCellProduct_ae_eq` — it agrees almost everywhere with the compensated
  product of the compensated integrals.
* `LevyStochCalc.Driver.measurable_levyCellProduct_comap` — measurability for the σ-algebra
  generated by the cell increment.
* `LevyStochCalc.Driver.memLp_levyCellProduct`, `LevyStochCalc.Driver.integral_levyCellProduct`,
  `LevyStochCalc.Driver.integral_levyCellProduct_mul` — square integrability, mean and Gram.
* `LevyStochCalc.Driver.integral_levyCellProfileStep_natAdd_mul_levyCellProduct` — orthogonality
  to the jump coordinates of the cell increment.
* `LevyStochCalc.Driver.integral_levyCellProfileStep_castAdd_mul_levyCellProduct` —
  orthogonality to the Brownian coordinates of the cell increment.
* `LevyStochCalc.Driver.aestronglyMeasurable_sigmaPoisson_compensatedProfileRepr`,
  `LevyStochCalc.Driver.aestronglyMeasurable_sigmaPoisson_compensatedProduct` — the jump
  coordinates of the cell increment and the compensated product are almost everywhere equal to
  functions measurable for the σ-algebra of the Poisson random measure.
* `LevyStochCalc.Driver.LevyDriver.integral_mul_eq_mul_integral_of_sigmaPoisson` — a function of
  the Brownian coordinates and a function of the Poisson random measure factor in expectation.
-/

